 "pupilsNote": "Frames with pupils as layers (neutral, ajar, wide, wide2): NEW - one layer per eye, <frame>_pupils_l / _pupils_r (viewer's left/right in the unmirrored file). Draw <frame>, then both eye layers at the same point; move each by the same look offset (dx, dy) from its own rest, then clamp the pupil CENTRE into that eye's travel ellipse: p = rest + d; q = (p - c) / radii; if |q| > 1: p = c + (q / |q|) * radii. All values in logical units from the feet (x right, y down, unmirrored; mirror/ceiling flips apply as for the frame) and in px of the 525x506 frame. whiteEllipse = fitted eye white; seam = the line between the eyes (no pupil pixel ever crosses it). The far (left) eye has a smaller travel - the 3/4 view. Left pupils rest moved off the seam (pupil.shiftFromOldPx). Other frames have the pupils baked in. | art-director-55 (2026-10-04): the rest of each pupil is now also the centre of its travel ellipse (pupils closer together: spacing 67-68% of the eye spacing); the code moves both pupils by ONE shift s = q * min(radii) from travel.center, so the spacing never changes with the look. l radii = the ellipse both eyes share (0.05 less), r radii = the same shared ellipse.",
